  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the set $B=(-\\infty ,\\sqrt{2}\\,].$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(B)$ and $sup(B).$The infimum of $B$ is the {{field-1}} of $B,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(B)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(B)$ {{field-6}}.",
